Privacy Policy

FixLog: Home Maintenance
Effective date: November 11, 2026

Developer: Technology Era

1. Introduction
Welcome to FixLog. Your privacy is important to us. FixLog is a home maintenance management application that helps users organize household appliances, track maintenance schedules, record repairs, and manage service history. This Privacy Policy explains how FixLog handles information when you use our application.

2. Information We Collect
FixLog is designed to work offline and does not require users to create an account. Depending on the features you use, the app may store the following information locally on your device: appliance names, brands, model numbers, categories, locations, photos selected by you, maintenance schedules, reminders, repair and service history, repair costs, currency preferences, notes, descriptions, and app preferences. This information is used to provide the application's features.

3. How Your Information Is Stored
Your appliance information, maintenance records, photos, and preferences are stored locally on your device. FixLog does not operate its own cloud database or require an online account for its core functionality. Your locally stored information remains on your device unless you delete it, clear the app's data, uninstall the application, or use another device-management feature that removes it.

4. Photos and Media
FixLog may request access to photos or media when you choose to add an appliance image or service attachment. Selected images are used only for the features you request and are stored locally, subject to your device's storage permissions and settings. FixLog does not intentionally upload these images to its own servers.

5. Notifications
FixLog may request permission to send local notifications. Notifications help remind you about upcoming, due, or overdue maintenance tasks. These reminders are generated by the application on your device. You can manage notification permissions through your device settings.

6. Data Sharing
FixLog does not sell your personal information. Information stored locally by the app is not intentionally shared with the developer or other parties through FixLog's core offline functionality. If future versions introduce advertising, analytics, crash reporting, or other third-party services, the relevant data handling practices will be disclosed in an updated Privacy Policy.

7. Data Security
We aim to protect your information by keeping core app records on your device. However, no storage method or electronic system can be guaranteed to be completely secure. We recommend keeping your device protected with an appropriate screen lock and maintaining backups of important information.

8. Data Retention and Deletion
FixLog does not maintain a developer-controlled account database for its offline features. You can remove your information by deleting individual appliances or service records within the app, using the Clear Data option if available, clearing the application's storage through your device settings, or uninstalling the application. Uninstalling the application or clearing its storage may permanently remove locally stored information.

9. Children's Privacy
FixLog is a general-purpose home management application and is not specifically designed to target children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children through our own servers.

10. Third-Party Services
The core functionality of FixLog is designed to operate offline. If third-party SDKs or services are included in a version of the application, such as advertising, analytics, or crash reporting tools, those services may process certain information according to their own privacy policies. Users should review the relevant third-party privacy policies where applicable.

11. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy when application features, legal requirements, or data-handling practices change. Any updated version will be made available through the application or its official privacy policy webpage.

